//# #2820 CONTROL. A field read on an unresolved type FORMAL stays tolerated,
//# because the same arm tolerates an unresolved CROSS-MODULE name on the
//# incremental per-file lane and this arm cannot tell the two apart.
//#
//# That tolerance is a known defect, not a decision -- #2848: `m.payload` on a
//# formal resolves by SPELLING against any struct declaring the name and reads
//# its offset, so `fn read[T](m: T) { m.payload }` applied to `7` answers `0`.
//# Fixing #2848 will have to change THIS file, and that is the intended signal.
//#
//# The second declaration is the one that keeps the `Map` half honest. A bare
//# type formal named for a builtin is legal, and it resolves to the same
//# `CtNamed("Map", [])` shape the builtin arrives as -- distinguished only by
//# arity, which is why the refusal requires the applied arity to match the
//# registry's (>= 1) rather than testing the name on its own.
struct Holder {
  v: Int
}

fn read[T](m: T) -> Int {
  m.v
}

fn shadowed[Map](m: Map) -> Int {
  7
}

export fn main() -> Int {
  read(Holder::{ v: 3 }) + shadowed(Holder::{ v: 1 })
}
